 "text": "Hi, how have you been? I like to use a wet room method and only apply varnish after the paint is completely dry. How thick you built up the paint layers affects this, oil based paints take a while. That's a tight turnaround, I'd re paint it if you' short on time. Use a thin coat of air dry lubricant oil paint instead? It's faster but still gives the benefit of oil. Dry touch free in about week, hold off washing for two weeks while the paint absorbs itself, and that's as dry as it gets.",
